{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Saving Painted Textures in Blender.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Saving Painted Textures in Blender.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"saving painted textures in blender saving painted textures in blender","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Saving Painted Textures in Blender.md","fileName":"Saving Painted Textures in Blender.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Saving Painted Textures in Blender","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-07 23:25\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Materials and Textures]] · [[Blender Texture Painting Workflow]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Materials and Textures","Blender Texture Painting Workflow","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf","creatinggameenvironmentsinblender3d.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Saving Painted Textures in Blender.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Saving Painted Textures in Blender.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"saving painted textures in blender saving painted textures in blender","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Saving Painted Textures in Blender.md","fileName":"Saving Painted Textures in Blender.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Saving Painted Textures in Blender","heading":"Saving Painted Textures in Blender","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A texture painted in Blender must be saved as an external image if it is to persist independently of the current in-memory image buffer. The Image Editor's Save As command chooses its location and format.\n\nThe UV layout can also be exported as an image, providing a guide for work in another painting application. A lossless format such as PNG preserves the painted result while keeping file size manageable.\n\nSaving is a separate step from painting because edits can remain only in Blender's image buffer. The artist should verify the active canvas and destination after a session so the material continues to find the intended image in later Blender or game-engine work.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Materials and Textures","Blender Texture Painting Workflow","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf","creatinggameenvironmentsinblender3d.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Saving Painted Textures in Blender.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Saving Painted Textures in Blender.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"saving painted textures in blender saving painted textures in blender","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Saving Painted Textures in Blender.md","fileName":"Saving Painted Textures in Blender.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Saving Painted Textures in Blender","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf]]\n\n[[creatinggameenvironmentsinblender3d.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Materials and Textures","Blender Texture Painting Workflow","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf","creatinggameenvironmentsinblender3d.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}